---
title: Digital Signature Flow - How Every Response is Secured
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as 👤 Client
    participant Server as 🖥️ Server
    participant Dilithium as 🔐 Dilithium Key Manager
    participant Signer as ✍️ Signing Service

    Note over Server,Dilithium: At server startup
    Server->>Dilithium: Generate key pair
    Dilithium-->>Server: Private key + Public key ready

    Note over Client,Signer: For every API response
    Client->>Server: Send request (e.g. create user)
    Server->>Server: Process the request
    Server->>Server: Build response data (Protocol Buffer)

    Server->>Signer: Sign this response
    Signer->>Signer: Serialize response to bytes
    Signer->>Dilithium: Sign these bytes with private key
    Dilithium-->>Signer: Digital signature
    Signer-->>Server: Signed response (data + signature)

    Server-->>Client: Return signed response

    Note over Client,Signer: Client can verify authenticity
    Client->>Server: GET /api/public-key
    Server-->>Client: Server's public key
    Client->>Client: Use public key to verify<br/>that the signature matches the data
    Client->>Client: If valid = data is authentic<br/>and has not been tampered with
